From ce63528500c86d5c84528ae608d118e3c8a1f44e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shorinkiwata <fcl709@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: Don't report unwritten write-copy pages as
 read-write.

VirtualProtect() replaced an old protection of PAGE_WRITECOPY with
PAGE_READWRITE unconditionally. Windows reports PAGE_READWRITE only for
write-copy pages that have been written (privately copied); pages that
were never written keep reporting PAGE_WRITECOPY, from VirtualQuery()
as well as the old protection returned by VirtualProtect(),
VirtualProtectEx() and NtProtectVirtualMemory(), which all agree.

ntdll reports written write-copy pages of image views as read-write by
itself when the kernel supports asynchronous userfaultfd write
protection, so on top of that the replacement only turned the correct
result for unwritten pages into a wrong one. For unwritten pages of
views mapped with FILE_MAP_COPY it returned a protection that can't be
set on such a view, so restoring the saved old protection failed where
it succeeds on Windows. It also made VirtualProtect() disagree with
VirtualProtectEx() on the current process.

Remove the replacement from kernelbase. Keep it in ntdll, for all
callers, only for image views whose writes are not tracked (the kernel
lacks support), where Wine still can't tell written pages apart.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/kernelbase/memory.c  | 4 +---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c | 8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/kernelbase/memory.c b/dlls/kernelbase/memory.c
index 99fc3e2d6d3..8c2d3542051 100644
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/memory.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/memory.c
@@ -583,9 +583,7 @@ BOOL WINAPI DECLSPEC_HOTPATCH  VirtualLock( void *addr, SIZE_T size )
  */
 BOOL WINAPI DECLSPEC_HOTPATCH VirtualProtect( void *addr, SIZE_T size, DWORD new_prot, DWORD *old_prot )
 {
-    BOOL ret = VirtualProtectEx( GetCurrentProcess(), addr, size, new_prot, old_prot );
-    if (old_prot && *old_prot == PAGE_WRITECOPY) *old_prot = PAGE_READWRITE;
-    return ret;
+    return VirtualProtectEx( GetCurrentProcess(), addr, size, new_prot, old_prot );
 }
 
 
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index 6e61f810970..8ca4905bcd9 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -6023,6 +6023,14 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtProtectVirtualMemory( HANDLE process, PVOID *addr_ptr, SIZE_T
                     set_page_vprot_bits(base, page_size, VPROT_COPIED, 0);
                 }
             }
+
+            /* Without write-copy tracking (see kernel_writecopy_track()) there is no
+             * telling whether an image page has been written. Keep reporting it as
+             * written then: code that makes its own initialized data read-only checks
+             * for PAGE_READWRITE as the old protection. */
+            if (status == STATUS_SUCCESS && old == PAGE_WRITECOPY &&
+                (view->protect & (SEC_IMAGE | VPROT_COPY_TRACKED)) == SEC_IMAGE)
+                old = PAGE_READWRITE;
         }
         else status = STATUS_NOT_COMMITTED;
     }
